cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Explainable residual CNN-Mamba hybrid for lung cancer histopathology:
  code, recovered LC25000 groups, splits and results
message: >-
  If you use this software or the data it releases, please cite it, together
  with the datasets it analyses (LC25000, LungHist700 and LC25000-clean; see
  README.md).
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Soni
    given-names: Meghraj
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Computer Science and Engineering, School of Studies of
      Engineering and Technology, Guru Ghasidas Vishwavidyalaya, Bilaspur, India
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9458-661X"
  - family-names: Sharma
    given-names: Suraj
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Computer Science and Engineering, School of Studies of
      Engineering and Technology, Guru Ghasidas Vishwavidyalaya, Bilaspur, India
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9403-9373"
repository-code: https://github.com/meghrajvyt/cnn-mamba-lung-histopathology
abstract: >-
  Code and released data for a leakage-controlled study of an explainable
  residual CNN-Mamba hybrid on lung histopathology: the architecture and its
  comparators, the recovery of the 716 LC25000 source-image groups, the
  LungHist700 patient-level folds, the external test, the measured
  explanation metrics (pathway attribution and deletion-insertion
  faithfulness), the cost benchmark, the cluster-aware statistics, and the
  scripts that regenerate every table and figure of the paper.
keywords:
  - lung cancer
  - histopathology
  - deep learning
  - state-space models
  - explainable artificial intelligence
  - data leakage
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-12"
